            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-28320",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-28320"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-28320?s=debian&n=curl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C%3D7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u13",
              "help": {
                "text": "A denial of service vulnerability exists in curl <v8.1.0 in the way libcurl provides several different backends for resolving host names, selected at build time. If it is built to use the synchronous resolver, it allows name resolves to time-out slow operations using `alarm()` and `siglongjmp()`. When doing this, libcurl used a global buffer that was not mutex protected and a multi-threaded application might therefore crash or otherwise misbehave.\n\n---\n- curl 7.88.1-10 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1036239; unimportant)\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2023-28320.html\nIntroduced by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3c49b405de4fbf1fd7127f91908261268640e54f (curl-7_9_8)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/13718030ad4b3209a7583b4f27f683cd3a6fa5f2 (curl-8_1_0)\nFollow-up: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/f446258f0269a62289cca0210157cb8558d0edc3 (curl-8_1_0)\nDebian binary package builds are not affected as the \"curl_jmpenv\" variable declaration was guarded\nby a \"#ifdef HAVE_SIGSETJMP\", but the variable would only be used on \"#ifdef USE_ALARM_TIMEOUT\". For\nDebian, \"HAVE_SIGSETJMP\" is true but \"USE_ALARM_TIMEOUT\" is false, and the threaded resolver is used.\n",
                "markdown": "> A denial of service vulnerability exists in curl <v8.1.0 in the way libcurl provides several different backends for resolving host names, selected at build time. If it is built to use the synchronous resolver, it allows name resolves to time-out slow operations using `alarm()` and `siglongjmp()`. When doing this, libcurl used a global buffer that was not mutex protected and a multi-threaded application might therefore crash or otherwise misbehave.\n\n---\n- curl 7.88.1-10 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1036239; unimportant)\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2023-28320.html\nIntroduced by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3c49b405de4fbf1fd7127f91908261268640e54f (curl-7_9_8)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/13718030ad4b3209a7583b4f27f683cd3a6fa5f2 (curl-8_1_0)\nFollow-up: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/f446258f0269a62289cca0210157cb8558d0edc3 (curl-8_1_0)\nDebian binary package builds are not affected as the \"curl_jmpenv\" variable declaration was guarded\nby a \"#ifdef HAVE_SIGSETJMP\", but the variable would only be used on \"#ifdef USE_ALARM_TIMEOUT\". For\nDebian, \"HAVE_SIGSETJMP\" is true but \"USE_ALARM_TIMEOUT\" is false, and the threaded resolver is used.\n\n|                                                                                                          |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <=7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13                                                                     |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<=7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-31437",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-31437"
