            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-14104",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-14104"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-14104?s=debian&n=util-linux&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C%3D2.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u2",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. This vulnerability allows a heap buffer overread when processing 256-byte usernames, specifically within the `setpwnam()` function, affecting SUID (Set User ID) login-utils utilities writing to the password database.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.41.3-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1122058; unimportant)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2419369\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/issues/3585\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/pull/3586\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/aaa9e718c88d6916b003da7ebcfe38a3c88df8e6\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/9a36d77012c4c771f8d51eba46b6e62c29bf572a\nAffected code in setpwnam() is only used by chsh and chfn which are not build\nin any Debian released binary package from src:util-linux and explicitly configured\nas with --disable-chfn-chsh since 2.25-1.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in util-linux. This vulnerability allows a heap buffer overread when processing 256-byte usernames, specifically within the `setpwnam()` function, affecting SUID (Set User ID) login-utils utilities writing to the password database.\n\n---\n- util-linux 2.41.3-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1122058; unimportant)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2419369\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/issues/3585\nhttps://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/pull/3586\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/aaa9e718c88d6916b003da7ebcfe38a3c88df8e6\nFixed by: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/9a36d77012c4c771f8d51eba46b6e62c29bf572a\nAffected code in setpwnam() is only used by chsh and chfn which are not build\nin any Debian released binary package from src:util-linux and explicitly configured\nas with --disable-chfn-chsh since 2.25-1.\n\n|                                                                                                              |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <=2.36.1-8+deb11u2                                                                            |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                     |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<=2.36.1-8+deb11u2",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-15079",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-15079"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-15079?s=debian&n=curl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C%3D7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u13",
              "help": {
                "text": "When doing SSH-based transfers using either SCP or SFTP, and setting the known_hosts file, libcurl could still mistakenly accept connecting to hosts *not present* in the specified file if they were added as recognized in the libssh *global* known_hosts file.\n\n---\n- curl 8.18.0~rc3-1 (unimportant)\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2025-15079.html\nIntroduced with: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/c92d2e14cfb0db662f958effd2ac86f995cf1b5a (curl-7_58_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/adca486c125d9a6d9565b9607a19dce803a8b479 (rc-8_18_0-3, curl-8_18_0)\nDebian builds with libssh2 for SSH backend\n",
                "markdown": "> When doing SSH-based transfers using either SCP or SFTP, and setting the known_hosts file, libcurl could still mistakenly accept connecting to hosts *not present* in the specified file if they were added as recognized in the libssh *global* known_hosts file.\n\n---\n- curl 8.18.0~rc3-1 (unimportant)\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2025-15079.html\nIntroduced with: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/c92d2e14cfb0db662f958effd2ac86f995cf1b5a (curl-7_58_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/adca486c125d9a6d9565b9607a19dce803a8b479 (rc-8_18_0-3, curl-8_18_0)\nDebian builds with libssh2 for SSH backend\n\n|                                                                                                          |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <=7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13                                                                     |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                 |\n"
              },
