            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-3576",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-3576"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-3576?s=debian&n=krb5&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C1.18.3-6%2Bdeb11u7",
              "help": {
                "text": "A vulnerability in the MIT Kerberos implementation allows GSSAPI-protected messages using RC4-HMAC-MD5 to be spoofed due to weaknesses in the MD5 checksum design. If RC4 is preferred over stronger encryption types, an attacker could exploit MD5 collisions to forge message integrity codes. This may lead to unauthorized message tampering.\n\n---\n- krb5 1.21.2-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1103525)\n[bookworm] - krb5 1.20.1-2+deb12u4\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2359465\nCVE relates to issues covered in:\nhttps://i.blackhat.com/EU-22/Thursday-Briefings/EU-22-Tervoort-Breaking-Kerberos-RC4-Cipher-and-Spoofing-Windows-PACs-wp.pdf\nSince upstream 1.21 (cf. https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/krb5-1.21/) the KDC\nwill no longer issue tickets with RC4 or triple-DES session keys unless\nexplicitly configured with the new allow_rc4 or allow_des3 variables respectively.\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/1b57a4d134bbd0e7c52d5885a92eccc815726463\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/2cbd847e0e92bc4e219b65c770ae33f851b22afc\n",
                "markdown": "> A vulnerability in the MIT Kerberos implementation allows GSSAPI-protected messages using RC4-HMAC-MD5 to be spoofed due to weaknesses in the MD5 checksum design. If RC4 is preferred over stronger encryption types, an attacker could exploit MD5 collisions to forge message integrity codes. This may lead to unauthorized message tampering.\n\n---\n- krb5 1.21.2-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1103525)\n[bookworm] - krb5 1.20.1-2+deb12u4\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2359465\nCVE relates to issues covered in:\nhttps://i.blackhat.com/EU-22/Thursday-Briefings/EU-22-Tervoort-Breaking-Kerberos-RC4-Cipher-and-Spoofing-Windows-PACs-wp.pdf\nSince upstream 1.21 (cf. https://web.mit.edu/kerberos/krb5-1.21/) the KDC\nwill no longer issue tickets with RC4 or triple-DES session keys unless\nexplicitly configured with the new allow_rc4 or allow_des3 variables respectively.\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/1b57a4d134bbd0e7c52d5885a92eccc815726463\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/2cbd847e0e92bc4e219b65c770ae33f851b22afc\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/krb5@1.18.3-6%2Bdeb11u3?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <1.18.3-6+deb11u7                                                                       |\n|Fixed version   1.18.3-6+deb11u7                                                                        |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.18.3-6+deb11u7",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
