                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-7264",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-7264"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-7264?s=debian&n=curl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u13",
              "help": {
                "text": "libcurl's ASN1 parser code has the `GTime2str()` function, used for parsing an ASN.1 Generalized Time field. If given an syntactically incorrect field, the parser might end up using -1 for the length of the *time fraction*, leading to a `strlen()` getting performed on a pointer to a heap buffer area that is not (purposely) null terminated.  This flaw most likely leads to a crash, but can also lead to heap contents getting returned to the application when [CURLINFO_CERTINFO](https://curl.se/libcurl/c/CURLINFO_CERTINFO.html) is used.\n\n---\n- curl 8.9.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1077656)\n[bookworm] - curl 7.88.1-10+deb12u7\n[bullseye] - curl 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2024-7264.html\nIntroduced by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3a24cb7bc456366cbc3a03f7ab6d2576105a1f2d (curl-7_32_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/27959ecce75cdb2809c0bdb3286e60e08fadb519 (curl-8_9_1)\n",
                "markdown": "> libcurl's ASN1 parser code has the `GTime2str()` function, used for parsing an ASN.1 Generalized Time field. If given an syntactically incorrect field, the parser might end up using -1 for the length of the *time fraction*, leading to a `strlen()` getting performed on a pointer to a heap buffer area that is not (purposely) null terminated.  This flaw most likely leads to a crash, but can also lead to heap contents getting returned to the application when [CURLINFO_CERTINFO](https://curl.se/libcurl/c/CURLINFO_CERTINFO.html) is used.\n\n---\n- curl 8.9.1-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1077656)\n[bookworm] - curl 7.88.1-10+deb12u7\n[bullseye] - curl 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2024-7264.html\nIntroduced by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/3a24cb7bc456366cbc3a03f7ab6d2576105a1f2d (curl-7_32_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/27959ecce75cdb2809c0bdb3286e60e08fadb519 (curl-8_9_1)\n\n|                                                                                                          |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "7.74.0-1.3+deb11u13",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-8096",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-8096"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-8096?s=debian&n=curl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u14",
              "help": {
                "text": "When curl is told to use the Certificate Status Request TLS extension, often referred to as OCSP stapling, to verify that the server certificate is valid, it might fail to detect some OCSP problems and instead wrongly consider the response as fine.  If the returned status reports another error than 'revoked' (like for example 'unauthorized') it is not treated as a bad certficate.\n\n---\n- curl 8.10.0-1\n[bookworm] - curl 7.88.1-10+deb12u8\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2024-8096.html\nIntroduced with: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/f13669a375f5bfd14797bda91642cabe076974fa (curl-7_41_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/aeb1a281cab13c7ba791cb104e556b20e713941f (curl-8_10_0)\n",
                "markdown": "> When curl is told to use the Certificate Status Request TLS extension, often referred to as OCSP stapling, to verify that the server certificate is valid, it might fail to detect some OCSP problems and instead wrongly consider the response as fine.  If the returned status reports another error than 'revoked' (like for example 'unauthorized') it is not treated as a bad certficate.\n\n---\n- curl 8.10.0-1\n[bookworm] - curl 7.88.1-10+deb12u8\nhttps://curl.se/docs/CVE-2024-8096.html\nIntroduced with: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/f13669a375f5bfd14797bda91642cabe076974fa (curl-7_41_0)\nFixed by: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/aeb1a281cab13c7ba791cb104e556b20e713941f (curl-8_10_0)\n\n|                                                                                                          |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <7.74.0-1.3+deb11u14                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   7.74.0-1.3+deb11u14                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<7.74.0-1.3+deb11u14",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "7.74.0-1.3+deb11u14",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u7?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
