            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61726",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61726"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-61726?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.24.12",
              "help": {
                "text": "The net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query.\n\nWhile the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption.\n",
                "markdown": "> The net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query.\n\nWhile the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.19.8  |\n|Affected range  <1.24.12                  |\n|Fixed version   1.24.12                   |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<1.24.12",
