            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4046",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-4046"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-4046?s=debian&n=glibc&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=11&vr=%3C%3D2.31-13%2Bdeb11u11",
              "help": {
                "text": "The iconv() function in the GNU C Library versions 2.43 and earlier may crash due to an assertion failure when converting inputs from the IBM1390 or IBM1399 character sets, which may be used to remotely crash an application.    This vulnerability can be trivially mitigated by removing the IBM1390 and IBM1399 character sets from systems that do not need them.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1132499)\n[trixie] - glibc <postponed> (Minor issue, revisit when fixed upstream)\n[bookworm] - glibc <postponed> (Minor issue, revisit when fixed upstream)\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=33980\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob_plain;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2026-0007\n",
                "markdown": "> The iconv() function in the GNU C Library versions 2.43 and earlier may crash due to an assertion failure when converting inputs from the IBM1390 or IBM1399 character sets, which may be used to remotely crash an application.    This vulnerability can be trivially mitigated by removing the IBM1390 and IBM1399 character sets from systems that do not need them.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1132499)\n[trixie] - glibc <postponed> (Minor issue, revisit when fixed upstream)\n[bookworm] - glibc <postponed> (Minor issue, revisit when fixed upstream)\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=33980\nhttps://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=blob_plain;f=advisories/GLIBC-SA-2026-0007\n\n|                                                                                                        |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/glibc@2.31-13%2Bdeb11u6?os_distro=bullseye&os_name=debian&os_version=11  |\n|Affected range  <=2.31-13+deb11u11                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                               |\n"
